│ patch_description        │ Replace the naive concentric-ring layout with a hexagonal grid layout (rows of 5,6,5,6,4  │
│                          │ circles = 26), which is the natural near-optimal structure for packing circles of similar │
│                          │ size, exploiting the hexagonal packing density locally. Then improve radius computation   │
│                          │ in two ways: (1) iterate the pairwise scaling passes until convergence instead of a       │
│                          │ single pass (a single pass under-scales radii badly since each pair adjustment            │
│                          │ invalidates earlier ones), and (2) add a gentle center-relaxation phase that pushes       │
│                          │ overlapping circle pairs apart while respecting the square boundary, letting the grid     │
│                          │ relax into the walls and fill corner gaps. This yields much larger radii while keeping    │
│                          │ the construction explicit and fully valid.                                                │
