│ patch_name               │ hexagonal_rows_packing                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the naive ring arrangement with a staggered hexagonal lattice pattern, which is   │
│                          │ the densest local arrangement for equal circles. Six rows with counts 5,4,5,4,5,3 (=26    │
│                          │ circles) are placed so horizontal neighbor spacing is 2r and vertical row spacing is      │
│                          │ sqrt(3)*r. The largest radius that fits vertically is r = 1/(5*sqrt(3)+2) ≈ 0.0938, and   │
│                          │ each row is inset by r from the walls so circles touch the square boundary tangentially.  │
│                          │ Equal radii are assigned directly (scaled by 0.999 for numerical safety), guaranteeing    │
│                          │ validity while raising the sum of radii from ~0.96 to ~2.44.                              │
