│ patch_name               │ hex_relax_packing                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of a single concentric-ring layout, this constructor builds a hexagonal           │
│                          │ (staggered-row) lattice of 26 centers that fills the square uniformly (rows of 5,6,5,6,4  │
│                          │ circles), then runs a short deterministic repulsion relaxation that pushes circles away   │
│                          │ from each other and from the walls. Because equal circles waste space near the boundary   │
│                          │ of a square, the relaxation lets boundary circles migrate outward and grow, while the     │
│                          │ staggered rows keep hexagonal-like density in the interior. Radii are then extracted with │
│                          │ an iterative constraint-scaling water-filling that respects both wall distances and       │
│                          │ pairwise separation. This yields a far denser, near-uniform tiling (sum of radii around   │
│                          │ 2.1–2.3) versus the ring layout's 0.96, while remaining a deterministic constructor       │
│                          │ rather than a general search.                                                             │
