│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hex_grid_growth_packing                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the naive concentric-ring layout with a hexagonal lattice layout of 26 circles    │
│                          │ (alternating rows of 5 and 6 circles, one dropped), which is the known optimal local      │
│                          │ structure for dense circle packing. Then replace the one-pass pairwise scaling radius     │
│                          │ computation with an iterative "shrink-to-constraint" growth algorithm: start each radius  │
│                          │ large and repeatedly shrink each radius to the minimum of (distance to walls) and         │
│                          │ (distance to each neighbor minus that neighbor's radius). This converges monotonically to │
│                          │ a valid packing where most circles touch either walls or neighbors, dramatically          │
│                          │ increasing the sum of radii (roughly 26 × 0.085 ≈ 2.2, versus the current 0.96).          │
