│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lp_refine_packing                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The prior best program (score 0.90, sum 2.37) used an exact LP for radii combined with a  │
│                          │ hill-climbing refinement of centers. The current program regressed to a fixed hexagonal   │
│                          │ layout with an ad-hoc iterative shrink (score 0.58, sum 1.52). The key insight: once      │
│                          │ centers are fixed, the maximum-radius assignment is a linear program (constraints r_i +   │
│                          │ r_j <= d_ij and r_i <= wall distances), and solving it exactly — rather than greedy       │
│                          │ shrinking — yields substantially larger sums. The remaining performance comes from local  │
│                          │ search over centers.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Improvements over the previous best version:                                              │
│                          │ 1. Vectorized LP constraint construction (much faster LP assembly → more refinement steps │
│                          │ within the time budget).                                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Multi-seed/multi-restart local search with simulated-annealing-style acceptance to     │
│                          │ escape local optima.                                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Better initial layout: staggered hex rows 5,6,5,6,4 plus a couple of alternative       │
│                          │ seeds.                                                                                    │
│                          │ 4. Final validity clipping to guarantee the packing is feasible (validity 1.00).          │
