│ patch_description        │ Instead of naive pairwise proportional radius shrinking, this approach: (1) initializes   │
│                          │ 26 centers on a staggered hexagonal lattice (rows 5,5,5,5,4,3) since hexagonal is         │
│                          │ near-optimal locally, (2) computes optimal radii for the given centers exactly via linear │
│                          │ programming (maximize sum r subject to r_i + r_j <= d_ij and r_i <= wall distance), and   │
│                          │ (3) iteratively refines centers using a deterministic "pressure" force (each circle is    │
│                          │ pushed away from its tightest contacts and walls), re-solving the LP after each           │
│                          │ refinement sweep. This alternating optimization (centers via geometric forces, radii via  │
│                          │ LP) is fundamentally different from the original one-shot proportional scaling and yields │
│                          │ a much larger, provably valid sum of radii.                                               │
