│ patch_description        │ The previous best program (2.36) used a true triangular-lattice layout with row spacing g │
│                          │ = s*sqrt(3)/2 (equilateral local geometry) and an exact LP for radii. The current program │
│                          │ regressed (2.02) by using uniform row/column spacing, which creates non-equilateral gaps. │
│                          │ I restore the triangular-lattice constructor, vectorize the LP constraint assembly with   │
│                          │ numpy broadcasting + scipy sparse matrices (per the identified bottleneck), and add a     │
│                          │ short randomized hill-climb on center positions: each step perturbs a few centers         │
│                          │ slightly, re-solves the LP, and keeps improvements. Vectorizing the LP makes each step    │
│                          │ cheap enough to fit many refinement iterations in the runtime budget, pushing sum of      │
│                          │ radii toward the 2.635 target.                                                            │
