│ patch_name               │ annealed_radii_maximizer                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of relying on a fixed geometric pattern plus blind repulsion (which plateaus at   │
│                          │ 1.60), this approach treats the packing as a continuous optimization problem: the         │
│                          │ objective is the sum of the maximum feasible (water-filled) radii, which is always valid  │
│                          │ by construction. Starting from a staggered hex grid, it runs simulated annealing directly │
│                          │ on circle centers — accepting moves with temperature-based probability, decaying          │
│                          │ temperature geometrically, with reheating when stuck. Because radii are recomputed as the │
│                          │ maximal feasible assignment after each move, every candidate is valid, so the optimizer   │
│                          │ can climb straight toward the 2.635 target rather than only pushing circles apart. A      │
│                          │ fixed RNG seed keeps the constructor deterministic. Vectorized radius computation keeps   │
│                          │ the runtime modest.                                                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
