│ patch_name               │ simulated_annealing_with_reheat                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current hill-climb only accepts strictly improving moves, so it gets stuck in local   │
│                          │ optima around 2.40. Replace it with simulated annealing: accept worse moves with          │
│                          │ probability exp((s_new - s_cur)/T), with T decaying geometrically. When no improvement    │
│                          │ occurs for ~50 accepted/evaluated steps, reheat by resetting T to its starting value (2–3 │
│                          │ times), then let it cool again. This lets circles pass through high-energy                │
│                          │ (overlapping-ish, small-radius) configurations to escape local optima, which is the key   │
│                          │ gap to 2.635. Also keep track of the best-ever configuration separately so annealing      │
│                          │ moves never degrade the returned answer.                                                  │
