│ patch_description        │ Restructures the solver into a three-stage pipeline: (1) a staggered hex-lattice seed     │
│                          │ generator, (2) an exact LP-based radius solver (maximize sum of radii subject to wall and │
│                          │ pairwise constraints) built with vectorized numpy broadcasting and a sparse CSR           │
│                          │ constraint matrix, and (3) a deterministic hill-climb that perturbs individual centers    │
│                          │ and re-solves the LP, accepting improvements. The LP replaces the suboptimal              │
│                          │ shrink-to-fit heuristic (which leaves slack on most circles), and the vectorized          │
│                          │ constraint assembly makes each LP solve fast enough to afford many hill-climb refinement  │
│                          │ steps within the time budget.                                                             │
