│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorized_lp_fast_hillclimb                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The bottleneck is the per-step LP re-solve (dense constraint assembly with Python loops). │
│                          │ This rewrite vectorizes the LP construction: pairwise indices via `np.triu_indices`,      │
│                          │ distances via one broadcasting call, and the constraint matrix as a                       │
│                          │ `scipy.sparse.csr_matrix`. This cuts per-step LP cost severalfold, allowing the           │
│                          │ hill-climb to run many more exact-LP- evaluated steps within the same runtime budget. I   │
│                          │ also keep the fast iterative radii solver as a cheap pre-screen (only accept candidate    │
│                          │ moves whose fast radii sum already beats the current one before paying for the LP), which │
│                          │ further increases effective step count. Multi-start over the same hex-row layouts is      │
│                          │ retained.                                                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0205                                                                                   │
