│ patch_name               │ add_row_and_cluster_shift_moves                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ All prior variants plateau at 2.36-2.40 because single-circle moves can't rearrange the   │
│                          │ lattice; the local triangular geometry forces every one-circle perturbation to be a net   │
│                          │ loss. The recommendation suggests rigid multi-circle moves: (1) translating an entire     │
│                          │ horizontal row of the hex layout by a small delta preserves all intra-row and most        │
│                          │ inter-row distances, letting rows collectively slide toward better wall alignment; (2)    │
│                          │ shifting a spatially coherent cluster (centers within 0.25 of a chosen circle) by a       │
│                          │ common delta moves a whole local patch rigidly. Both moves keep the LP radii valid and    │
│                          │ are accepted only if the LP total improves, so correctness is guaranteed. I add these     │
│                          │ move types with ~10% probability each into the existing hill climb, alongside the current │
│                          │ single-circle slack-directed move (applied the remaining ~80% of the time). I also        │
│                          │ slightly reduce the per-move LP cost by keeping the same time budget (1.6 s).             │
