│ patch_description        │ The current seed screen only runs 2 of 5 layouts, and the seed list contains              │
│                          │ [5,4,5,4,5,3]... actually [5,6,5,6,4] and [6,5,6,5,4] both — but the real issue is we     │
│                          │ only test 2 layouts with dense exact-LP steps (300 each). The hill-climb converges        │
│                          │ quickly (since_gain restart after 60), so 300 steps is more than enough per layout. We    │
│                          │ should instead screen many more distinct seed geometries cheaply using fast_radii, and    │
│                          │ only run the full LP hill-climb on the top 2-3. Since local search dominates runtime,     │
│                          │ screening 10-15 seeds with fast_radii costs microseconds and lets us pick genuinely       │
│                          │ better starting basins. Distinct row structures like [6,5,4,5,6], boundary-heavy          │
│                          │ variants, and vertical/y-scale variations (0.96, 1.02) explore different local optima —   │
│                          │ AlphaEvolve's best n=26 packings favor dense boundary rows with a hexagonal core. This    │
│                          │ increases multi-start diversity without increasing runtime much, which should push        │
│                          │ sum_radii above 2.37.                                                                     │
