│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ annealed_acceptance_reheat_hillclimb                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current hill-climb only accepts strictly improving moves, so it gets trapped in the   │
│                          │ first local optimum it reaches — likely far below AlphaEvolve's 2.635 (we're at 2.37).    │
│                          │ The previously validated insight from the program history is that stochastic scheduling   │
│                          │ (adaptive step sizes) already helped; the natural extension is Metropolis-style           │
│                          │ acceptance of slightly worse moves at temperature T, geometrically decaying, with         │
│                          │ reheating after a streak of rejections to escape local basins. I add a `best` snapshot    │
│                          │ (best centers/radii/sum) so worse exploratory moves never cost us the final answer, decay │
│                          │ T from 0.01 to 1e-4, reheat after 50 consecutive non-improving acceptances (capped at 2   │
│                          │ reheats, restoring the best configuration), and adaptively grow the step when moves are   │
│                          │ rejected so the search doesn't stall. All moves are still validated by the exact LP, so   │
│                          │ validity stays at 1.00.                                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0138                                                                                   │
