│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorized_sparse_lp_and_prescreen                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current hill-climb spends most of its 1.2s budget on the LP re-solve, but the LP is   │
│                          │ built with a Python double loop over all 325 pairs plus dense constraint matrices — very  │
│                          │ slow per iteration, so few moves are evaluated. Two targeted improvements: (1) build the  │
│                          │ LP constraint matrix vectorized via numpy (triu_indices for pairs) and pass it as a scipy │
│                          │ sparse CSR matrix, cutting LP setup cost by ~20-50x; (2) add a cheap vectorized           │
│                          │ "water-fill" pre-screen (fast_radii) so only moves that improve the fast proxy pay the LP │
│                          │ cost, roughly tripling the number of evaluated moves in the same time budget. Both        │
│                          │ directly implement the recommendation of slack-directed targeted moves being more likely  │
│                          │ accepted and address wasted evaluations.                                                  │
