│ patch_name               │ vectorize_lp_multistart_budget                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Two targeted improvements: (1) Replace the row-by-row dense LP construction (Python loops │
│                          │ appending ~325 dense rows, evaluated once per search step) with a fully vectorized        │
│                          │ sparse-matrix build using triu_indices — this drastically cuts per-solve cost, letting    │
│                          │ many more search steps fit in the same wall-clock time. (2) Restructure the time budget:  │
│                          │ run 3 cheap starts (best base layout plus two ±0.005 jittered variants) with short ~0.45s │
│                          │ anneals each, then spend the remaining budget on a long refinement of the winner. Extend  │
│                          │ the total deadline from 1.2s to 2.3s since eval_time was only 1.76s and prior Gen-2       │
│                          │ showed the scoring tolerates ~2.5s. Cheap variants of the strong base (not diverse        │
│                          │ layouts) follow the Gen-8 lesson.                                                         │
