│ patch_name               │ force_relaxed_multistart_lp                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of enumerating rigid hex-row templates, this approach uses a physical relaxation  │
│                          │ search: multiple starting configurations (hex grids with random jitter plus fully random  │
│                          │ starts), then an iterative force-based refinement. Each iteration (1) solves the exact LP │
│                          │ for optimal radii given the current centers, (2) computes repulsion forces between circle │
│                          │ pairs whose distance constraint is nearly tight and inward forces from nearly-tight       │
│                          │ walls, (3) moves centers accordingly. This lets the packing deform away from rigid        │
│                          │ templates toward the true optimum (where variable radii let circles of different sizes    │
│                          │ interlock), while the LP guarantees exact optimal radii at every step. The LP assembly is │
│                          │ vectorized with a sparse matrix for speed, enabling hundreds of relaxation steps within   │
│                          │ budget. Best (centers, radii) found across all starts and all iterations is returned.     │
