│ patch_name               │ multi_start_jittered_hillclimb                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single-trajectory simulated annealing (which regressed to 2.38 from the 2.40  │
│                          │ greedy hill-climb) with a multi-start greedy hill-climb: each of 4 starts begins from the │
│                          │ best lattice candidate perturbed with a distinct ±0.01 Gaussian jitter, and the time      │
│                          │ budget is split evenly with shrinking per-start deadlines                                 │
│                          │ ((deadline−now)/(n_starts−start)). The hill-climb itself keeps the LP re-solve and        │
│                          │ adaptive step-size shrink/grow schedule that previously broke 2.40. Jittered variants of  │
│                          │ a strong base have empirically beaten diverse layouts, and decorrelating the starts       │
│                          │ cheaply samples more basins within the same wall-clock time. Also expand the seed         │
│                          │ candidate list slightly so the base itself is stronger before jittering.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
