│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ prescreened_hillclimb_packing                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign replacing the exhaustive layout-enumeration + LP scoring with a       │
│                          │ seeded stochastic hill-climb over circle positions. A cheap vectorized greedy radius      │
│                          │ solver (`compute_max_radii`) acts as a pre-screen for every trial move; the exact LP      │
│                          │ (`_lp_radii`) is only invoked when the greedy sum beats the incumbent's greedy sum minus  │
│                          │ a small margin, drastically cutting LP calls. The search starts from multiple hex-lattice │
│                          │ seeds (different row compositions and stagger patterns) and perturbs individual circle    │
│                          │ coordinates, keeping the best (centers, radii) found. This data-flow change (greedy       │
│                          │ screen → selective LP) lets the constructor explore far more configurations within the    │
│                          │ time budget, pushing sum_radii well above the previous 2.25 while retaining validity via  │
│                          │ the exact LP solution.                                                                    │
